{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Big Decisions", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "A Clear Path Ahead", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 18, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about backgrounds in a wider variety of communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le18ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Explaining and Organizing Your Opinions, and Encouraging Agreement", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use words like <span class=\"italic\">think</span> and <span class=\"italic\">seem</span> to express your opinions and questions to encourage agreement.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use phrases like:<span class=\"italic\"><ul><li> I think ...</li><li>You seem ...</li><li>It seems ...</li></ul></span>to explain your opinion.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">You seem to be great at that!    </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use questions and questions within sentences to encourage agreement.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">Didn't he like your concept?<br/>So you think he's agreeable to your plan.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Didn't he like your concept?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "So you think he's agreeable to your plan.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "But you think that he is considering it. So that's really encouraging!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I don't think it went as well as I hoped.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You seem to be great at that!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I don't think it went as well as I hoped. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Modals for Speculation, Possibility and Necessity", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<p>When you speculate about something, you are making a guess based on what you know about the situation.</p><p>You use modals when you want to express possibility and necessity.</p>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can show you are speculating about something by using a modal, like <span class=\"italic\">must</span>, <span class=\"italic\">might</span>, <span class=\"italic\">may </span>or <span class=\"italic\">could</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The modal verb is followed by the main verb in the base form. You do not use \u201c<span class=\"italic\">to</span>\u201d. Do not add \u201c<span class=\"italic\">ing</span>\u201d, \u201c<span class=\"italic\">ed</span>\u201d, or \u201c<span class=\"italic\">s</span>\u201d to the verb.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <span class=\"italic\">He <span class=\"strong\">must like</span> the idea a bit.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">You use <span class=\"italic\">may</span>, <span class=\"italic\">might</span> and <span class=\"italic\">could</span> to express possibility in the past and in the future.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "*<span class=\"italic\">Might </span>suggests that something is less possible than <span class=\"italic\">may</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">might </span>/ <span class=\"italic\">might not</span> + infinitive</li><li><span class=\"italic\">could </span>/ <span class=\"italic\">could not</span> + infinitive</li><li><span class=\"italic\">may </span>/ <span class=\"italic\">may not</span> + infinitive</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <span class=\"italic\">He might want to renovate the restaurant.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Expressing Necessity</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">must </span>or <span class=\"italic\">have to</span> to express that something is necessarily true. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You have got to be proud of yourself.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He must like the idea a bit.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He might want to renovate the restaurant. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "That could be very costly.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You have to weigh your options very carefully.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to weigh one's options", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to consider options in order to judge which one is the best one", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You don't want to make any hasty decisions about decorating. That could be very costly. You have to weigh your options very carefully.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le18ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words to review.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "hasty ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "moving or acting very fast without paying much attention or thinking things over", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You don't want to make any hasty decisions about decorating.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le18ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to keep an open mind", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be open and listen to all the ideas and opinions about something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I don't think it went as well as I hoped. I'm a bit discouraged but I'm going to keep an open mind. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le18ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "concept ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a structured idea that has been thought over beforehand", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: What did he say about changing the style of the restaurant? Didn't he like your concept?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le18ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "impulsive ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "acting quickly without giving things much of a thought", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He's not impulsive so he's going to take some time to mull it over.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le18ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to mull over", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to take time for thinking about a problem or situation carefully", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He's not impulsive so he's going to take some time to mull it over.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le18ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to bounce ideas off", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to tell someone about an idea in order to know that person's opinion", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'd like to bounce some decorating ideas off of you before I order new furniture and paint!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le18ob11aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to take the plunge", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to suddenly commit oneself to something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'd like to bounce some decorating ideas off of you before I take the plunge and order new furniture and paint!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le18ob11aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about feelings, reactions and decision-making.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I explain my opinions and encourage agreement.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I speculate about things and express possibility and necessity.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I role-play a career counsellor and employee.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Imagine that you are considering a change to a completely different career or job.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down at least three reasons that you want to make this change.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Role-play a conversation with a career counsellor who will ask you questions to help you make a decision. Your partner will be the career counsellor.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The career counsellor needs to be prepared to ask questions that will help the employee make the right decision.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Change roles with and partner and repeat the activity.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about feelings, reactions, and decision making.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can explain opinions and encourage agreement.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can speculate about things and express possibility and necessity.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " How would you help a friend or family member make an important decision?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Do you think there are times when a person should make their own decisions without any help? When?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Let's review!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "id": 0}, {"questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "t